---
export const title = 'Streaming and citations';
export const order = 250;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  For an answer that arrives in pieces, set <code>streaming</code> and keep replacing
  <code>value</code> with the text so far. Only the last blocks are parsed again, so a long answer
  costs the same per piece as a short one. An unfinished <code>**</code>, <code>`</code> or link at the
  end shows as it will once complete, and a caret marks the end. Turn <code>streaming</code> off when
  the answer is complete; the finished text is then rendered exactly as written.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-markdown id='markdown-stream' size='sm' streaming></wc-markdown>
  <wc-button id='markdown-stream-replay' variant='text' size='sm' style='margin-top: 0.75rem;'>Play again</wc-button>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var answer =
        'Desk support in Pune has **2 loaner laptops** free[1](cite:asset_9). ' +
        'Incidents raised before noon are usually handled the same day[2](cite:sla_3).\n\n' +
        '- Raise the incident with the asset tag\n' +
        '- Pick the loaner up at desk 4 on the second floor\n\n' +
        'Your leave starts **Friday**, so raise it today.';
      var el = document.querySelector('#markdown-stream');
      el.citations = [
        { id: 'asset_9', headline: 'Loaner pool · Pune', supportingText: 'Asset management', href: '#asset-9' },
        { id: 'sla_3', headline: 'Hardware incident SLA', supportingText: 'Knowledge base' },
      ];
      var timer;
      function play() {
        clearInterval(timer);
        var shown = 0;
        el.streaming = true;
        el.value = '';
        timer = setInterval(function () {
          shown = Math.min(answer.length, shown + 3 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 6));
          el.value = answer.slice(0, shown);
          if (shown >= answer.length) {
            clearInterval(timer);
            el.streaming = false;
          }
        }, 60);
      }
      document.querySelector('#markdown-stream-replay').addEventListener('click', play);
      play();
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  Streams from Peacock's AI provider are <code>AsyncIterable&lt;string&gt;</code>.
  <code>readStream()</code> joins the pieces and reports the text at most once a frame:
</p>

<pre><code>import {'{ readStream }'} from '@redvars/peacock';

markdown.streaming = true;
await readStream(provider.summarize(request), (text, done) => {'{'}
  markdown.value = text;
  markdown.streaming = !done;
{'}'}, signal);</code></pre>

<h3 class="text-title-medium">Citations</h3>
<p>
  Links written as <code>[2](cite:rule_88)</code> show as <code>wc-citation</code> chips.
  <code>citations</code> gives each source's <code>headline</code>, <code>supportingText</code> and
  <code>href</code> by <code>id</code>; <code>citation-href</code> (with <code>{'{id}'}</code>) is the
  address of a source it doesn't list. A <code>cite:</code> link is never an ordinary link, so an
  answer can't send someone to an address the model made up.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-markdown
    size='sm'
    citation-href='#source-{id}'
    value='Exports failed because the retry limit was `0`[1](cite:inc_2041). Ravi raised it to 5 in 4.2.1[2](cite:comment_17).'
  ></wc-markdown>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3 class="text-title-medium">Accessibility</h3>
<p>
  While <code>streaming</code> is on, the content is <code>aria-busy</code>, so screen readers wait for
  the finished text instead of reading every piece. The caret is hidden from them, and it stops
  blinking with reduced motion.
</p>
